I. Adding the meta-unipi layer to your build
=================================================

Run 'bitbake-layers add-layer meta-unipi-eol'

II. Misc
========
Variables to modify behavior of eol test

- UNIPI_EOL_IMAGENAME_CMD
  The variable contains a command that is run while performing the image-info service and should display the image name on the standard output

- UNIPI_EOL_IMAGEVERSION_CMD
  The variable contains a command that is run while performing the image-info service and should display the image version on the standard output

- UNIPI_EOL_POSTEXEC_CMD
  The variable contains a command that can run after the image-info service ends.  Command is inserted to unit definition as
  ExecPostStop=..., so command must be expressed with full path or use /bin/sh -c '....'.
  Default is /bin/true.

- UNIPI_EOL_BUILD_INSTALL_CMD
  This command is executed when generating the image-info package not in the runtime. The string is inserted into the install() function.
  The working directory and destination directory ${D} need to be taken into account.


! Do not use " and # in variables, They are pre-processed by sed!

Service image-info.service is installed into /etc/systemd/system or
into ${OVERLAYFS_ETC_MOUNT_POINT}/overlay-etc/systemd/system if variable OVERLAYFS_ETC_MOUNT_POINT is defined.
This service runs during the first boot. It waits for expected network, collects informations about image and
sends it to predefined api. Finally, the service is disabled and removed regardless of the result of the service running.
